    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, you mentioned the border and this is something that bothers me quite a bit because there's a lot of conversations at the southern border and it's like, oh, it's either 100% of humanitarian crisis or 100% of border security crisis. And I think there's a lot of politicians who just refuse to use nuance and try to come together to solve it. I also don't hear a lot from just as an example, blue state governors saying, hey, you know, fentanyl coming up is killing people on our streets. And I don't know. I mean, why do you think it is that you don't have more governors vocally speaking up about the security issue at the southern border, given that it is directly contributing to so many of these drugs coming in and killing people in our communities?",
