    "turn_idx": 70,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, but when it comes to drug trafficking, and you guys have had some big busts out here, we've had some big busts over in King County involving, I mean, enough fentanyl pills in one of them to kill every person in King County, enough doses of fentanyl, which is insane. And you mentioned it earlier. Each one of those pills is like, to me, attempted homicide, it's attempted murder. And so if I'm a cartel member, okay, I'm just thinking, why would I not traffic drugs through Washington? why would I not in this political climate? The police pursuit law, where it made it almost impossible for police to pull someone over. If I'm a cartel person, I'm like, wow, I can just, I could bring drugs in, just flee when the police try to pull me over, if it comes down to that, and I'm off scot free. So I guess what can we, that's a stupid question, but what can we do in this state to make it a less appealing place for the Mexican cartel to",
