    "turn_idx": 109,
    "turn_text": "heard something a couple months ago. Some spokesman, I think it was for the Department of Ecology, they were responding to a question of why is this system not put together? And I can't quote them directly, but essentially the gist of it was, well, the rules are there. We're anticipating that the distributors, the dealers, they come up with a system in order to keep track of all this and report to us. And I'm thinking, Really? That's how state government works that we just allow those people that we decided to tax to tell us how they're collecting it and when they're going to turn it in. There's got to be more guidance than that. So it's total confusion out there. It really is. You're right. Agriculture is supposed to be exempt. However, there's a huge fine on the distributors if they don't collect the tax that they're supposed to be. So they're not going to error on the side of getting fined. They're going to be very cautious and make sure that they collect whether you should have been taxed or not. They're going to tax you so that they're not putting a position of paying a huge $10,000 a day of fine. And so then you've got to work it out afterward. You know this the whole concept of this thing even though we were promised by Many people in the in the administration that oh you want me to notice",
