  {
    "episode_id": 49122,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49122.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 113,
    "turn_text": "I think they knew what they were doing. When you increase taxes on anything, you see a direct correlation to consumption. If cost of something goes up, consumption of that item usually goes down. And like I said, this is just part of the strategy to wean the American public. And of course, we're leading as a state of Washington. We're going to single-handedly win this fight on CO2. We're going to, by increasing the cost of fossil fuels, change people's consumption habits and move to other sources of energy. And I think that's their goal. And by increasing those costs, I think they knew right up front that it was going to exactly do what's happening today. And to be telling us and selling it is something that you not even going to notice was very disingenuous. And then, you know, if they had, you know, maybe we'd still disagree with them. Maybe they'd have a little more credibility, but that being the ultimate goal of increasing the price because of the consumption issues, I think they've been very disingenuous to the Washington State public, and they should be held accountable for that.",
