  {
    "episode_id": 49122,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49122.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 143,
    "turn_text": "Well, that seems easy enough to do that, make that statement. But there are a lot of, it's complicated. Investments in companies sometimes get very hard to determine who's who and what are the origins. There's a lot of, I guess you could say, levels of ownership in these big companies. And so sometimes it's not as easy as you think. And like I said, there's not a good system of reporting. If there's the assessor's office in Yakima County gets paperwork, there's some kind of land deal going on. How does that get reported to the USDA or the Department of Treasury? There's no system to do that. So we're trying to put together, like I said, give these agencies the resources, the tools, come up with the system to put into place to prevent this.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
