  {
    "episode_id": 49122,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49122.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 162,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, there were only two of us out of the 10 that survived. For a lot of different reasons, some decided just to retire, redistricting impacted some people's decision. That's a good question. I think There are so many issues that are important that we need to focus on for my constituents, things that are important in Central Washington, some of the things that we've just talked about, whether it's fentanyl or China, or prices of gasoline, those kinds of things. I've not been solely focused on January 6th. I've made that decision. I would make it again today. But I think that it behooves us as Congress to be focused on those things that truly impact Americans now and in their future. And I want to make sure that we are in the strongest position possible as a nation. Our economy is strong. People are working. People feel good about their futures. And to do that, you can't dwell on the past and things that we've already made decisions on. So we're looking forward to those things that we need to solve, the problems that we face Americans and working on solutions.",
